From 8b1759f345aaafcc0cbe7dcaa6bb1102b0393565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petar Kirov <petar.p.kirov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:35:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [SPIRV] Lower a peeled cbuffer array to an array of its
 element

A cbuffer array whose stride is wider than its element is represented as
{[N-1 x <{T, spirv.Padding}>], T}. It was lowered to an array of the padded
struct {T, i8}, which declares an 8-bit member (and with it Int8 and 8-bit
storage) and gives the array a different type from the T[N] the source
declared.

Lower it to OpTypeArray T N with the padded element's size as its
ArrayStride: the padding is the distance between elements, never a member.
Accesses follow: a GEP over the padded element indexes the array of T
directly, dropping the index that selected T inside its padding, and a byte
offset into the peeled array divides by the stride, the last element
included. The member pointer keeps the peeled type, so the access chain and
the variable agree on one array type.
